= TH Layout Rigs =

"""What a shot's layout animates on the stage: a rig per character, a control per other asset, the camera rig."""

With the project setting *Layout in Animate (Beta)* on, layout animates the
shot in an APEX Animate LOP after this node.

* *rig*: an asset with a rig published loads it under `/layout_rigs/<name>`
  (its shape only), started at its layout placement; the asset's own prim is
  hidden while layout works.
* *control*: any other asset gets a placement control on its own prim. USD
  keys already on it become the control's channels.
* *off*: left as it is.

Then the shot camera: the camera rig a package registered (TumbleRig's), else
SideFX's camera rig on `/cameras/render_camera`.

@parameters

Discover:
    Fill the rows from the input stage, keeping the mode and version of
    prims already listed.

Build:
    Rebuild the network inside (dive) from the rows.

Rows:
    One per asset prim: its prim, asset, mode, rig channel and version.
